## Collected text is not covered by this licence

The Dutch corpus in `tests/corpora/` also holds paragraphs collected from elsewhere,
marked `origin: collected`. **Each of those stays under the licence it arrived under,
held by whoever wrote it**, and every entry carries that licence, its source and a
resolvable url in its own record. Nothing here relicenses them and nothing here makes
them this project's data.

This matters in both directions. A CC BY 3.0 paragraph stays CC BY 3.0: that licence
has no upgrade clause, so redistributing it verbatim as CC BY 4.0 would not be
permitted, and the per-entry licence field is what keeps it from being claimed as such.
And the attribution a reuser owes is owed to the original author rather than to this
project, so an entry has to record who wrote the text and not only where it was found.

